# One speedup per commit. Adapt the type(scope) prefix and the subject limit to
# the target project's convention (its AGENTS.md / CLAUDE.md). Lines beginning
# with '#' are stripped by git. Wrap the body at 72 columns. State the measured
# problem and the measured result, not a narration of the diff.

<type>(<scope>) <imperative summary of the single change>

why: <the measured problem this fixes: what was slow and by how much, e.g.
     "make_config ran 40x at function scope (~0.3s each, ~12s of setup)">

what:
- <the single change applied>
- <measured delta: suite X.Xs -> Y.Ys (-Z%), above the k*MAD noise band>
